# API Overview

The Price Books API provides full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) functionality for price books and price book entries within an organization.

Price books in Salesforce Commerce Cloud contain the pricing information for products. They can be organized in hierarchies where one price book can inherit from another (parent) price book. Each price book is associated with a specific currency and can be assigned to one or more sites.

Price book entries define the actual prices for products within a price book. Each entry carries one or more price scale tables, and each table has its own validity window and a set of quantity-based tiers (as absolute monetary amounts or percentage discounts). Entries have a composite identity of (priceBookId, productId).

## Authentication & Authorization

For resource access, you must use a client ID and client secret from Account Manager to request an access token. The access token is used as a bearer token and added to the Authorization header of your API request.

You must include `sfcc.price-books` (read-only access) or `sfcc.price-books.rw` (read-write access) in the client ID used to generate the token. For a full list of required permissions, see the [Authorization Scopes Catalog.](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/guide/auth-z-scope-catalog.html)

For detailed setup instructions, see the Authorization for Admin APIs guide.

## Response Details

### Timeouts

Admin API requests must respond within 60 seconds. If a response exceeds this threshold, an HTTP 504 status code is returned. For details, see [Timeouts and Limits.](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/guide/timeouts-limits.html)

### Error Handling

Error responses follow the [RFC 7807](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7807) problem detail format. To trace errors, include a `correlation-id` header in your request — the response returns it as `x-correlation-id`. For details, see [HTTP Status Codes and Errors.](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/guide/error-response-codes.html)

## Key Constraints

- **Currency Immutability**: The currency code of a price book is immutable after creation. PATCH attempts to change it will be rejected.
- **Parent Cycles**: Parent price book relationships that would create a cycle are rejected server-side.
- **Site Assignments**: The `siteAssignments` field on a price book is read-only. Assignments are managed via the site-assignment endpoints on this API (`PUT`/`DELETE /price-books/{priceBookId}/site-assignments/{siteId}`).
- **Price Tables**: The `priceTables` array in price book entries is replaced wholesale on PATCH; individual tables and their tiers cannot be updated independently.
- **Price Book Type**: A price book with `type: feed_based` has its price entries sourced from an external feed pipeline. The price book container itself remains editable via this API, but price book entry write operations against a feed-based price book are rejected.

## Use Cases

### Create a Price Book
Create a new price book with a specific currency. The price book ID is client-supplied and immutable, so creation uses `PUT` with the ID in the path (create-or-replace upsert); there is no `POST` collection endpoint:
```json
PUT /organizations/{organizationId}/price-books/USD-list-prices
{
  "id": "USD-list-prices",
  "displayName": "USD List Prices",
  "currencyCode": "USD",
  "online": true,
  "validFrom": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "validTo": "2024-12-31T23:59:59.999Z"
}
```

### Add a Price to a Product
Create or update a price book entry with a single amount tier:
```json
PUT /organizations/{organizationId}/price-books/{priceBookId}/price-book-entries/{productId}
{
  "productId": "product-001",
  "priceTables": [
    {
      "tiers": [
        { "type": "amount", "quantity": 1, "amount": { "currencyMnemonic": "USD", "value": 99.99 } }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "online": true
}
```

### Configure Tiered Pricing
Set up time-scoped quantity-based pricing, mixing absolute amounts and percentage discounts:
```json
PUT /organizations/{organizationId}/price-books/{priceBookId}/price-book-entries/{productId}
{
  "productId": "product-002",
  "priceTables": [
    {
      "validFrom": "2026-11-25T00:00:00.000Z",
      "validTo": "2026-11-28T23:59:59.999Z",
      "tiers": [
        { "type": "amount", "quantity": 1,  "amount": { "currencyMnemonic": "USD", "value": 39.99 } },
        { "type": "amount", "quantity": 10, "amount": { "currencyMnemonic": "USD", "value": 34.99 } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "validFrom": "2026-12-01T00:00:00.000Z",
      "tiers": [
        { "type": "amount",     "quantity": 1,  "amount": { "currencyMnemonic": "USD", "value": 49.99 } },
        { "type": "percentage", "quantity": 10, "percentage": 15.0 }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "online": true
}
```

### Find Active Price Books
Search for price books that are currently active (online) and valid:
```json
{
  "query": {
    "boolQuery": {
      "must": [
        {
          "termQuery": {
            "fields": ["online"],
            "operator": "is",
            "values": [true]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### Search by Currency
Find all price books for a specific currency:
```json
{
  "query": {
    "termQuery": {
      "fields": ["currencyCode"],
      "operator": "is",
      "values": ["USD"]
    }
  },
  "sorts": [
    {
      "field": "displayName",
      "sortOrder": "asc"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Text Search
Search for price books by name or description:
```json
{
  "query": {
    "textQuery": {
      "fields": ["id", "displayName", "description"],
      "searchPhrase": "sale"
    }
  }
}
```

